Description: GHSA-v8xr-gpvj-cx9g (CVE-2025-1217), GHSA-pcmh-g36c-qc44 (CVE-2025-1734), GHSA-52jp-hrpf-2jff (CVE-2025-1861) and GHSA-hgf5-96fm-v528 (CVE-2025-1736) for PHP 5.6: the http:// stream wrapper reads the response headers as PHP 7.4 and later do: a folded header (a line that starts with a space or a tab) is joined to the header before it, a header line without a colon, with a space in the header name, starting with a CR or folded before the first header fails the request, a Location header is followed with up to 8182 bytes (5.6 cut it at 1024 bytes) and fails the request when longer, and an Authorization or Proxy-Authorization header of the user is seen only at the start of a header line, so that the one made from the user:password of the URL is no longer left out when the name appears inside another header; with the bounds fixes of GH-23467 (CVE-2026-93682) and GH-23521 for a relative Location. An empty Location header is not followed, as before in 5.6 (7.4 and later go to /).
Origin: port of php-src commits bf4a8df2b397 (31.12.2024), 0b965cf85f51 (19.01.2025), 134f821622e2 (14.02.2025) and 5418040dcaac (04.03.2025, all Jakub Zelenka), f4897028a4bb (24.08.2026, Ilia Alshanetsky) and bd7e19b216c2 (31.08.2026, Jordi Kroon) of the PHP 7.4 security branch of Remi Collet (remicollet/php-src-security PHP-7.4-security-backports), with their tests and bug47021.phpt and bug75535.phpt of that branch (5.6 had neither), and ext/standard/tests/http/ServerClientTestCase.inc of that branch without the type declarations PHP 5 does not have; the ghsa-hgf5 tests read the request up to its empty line, as 5.6 sends it in several writes; http_empty_location_no_redirect.phpt is ours

